## YARN (Yet Another Resource Negotiator)

### YARN Architecture

YARN separates resource management from job scheduling and monitoring.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│        ResourceManager (RM)             │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐│
│  │ Scheduler  │  ApplicationsManager   ││
│  │ - Allocate │  - Lifecycle mgmt      ││
│  │   resources│  - Restart failed apps ││
│  └─────────────────────────────────────┘│
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
           ↓
    ┌──────┴──────┬──────────────┐
    ↓             ↓              ↓
┌─────────┐ ┌─────────┐ ┌─────────────┐
│NodeMgr 1│ │NodeMgr 2│ │  NodeMgr N  │
│ ┌─────┐ │ │ ┌─────┐ │ │ ┌─────────┐ │
│ │Cont1│ │ │ │Cont1│ │ │ │Cont1..N │ │
│ └─────┘ │ │ └─────┘ │ │ └─────────┘ │
└─────────┘ └─────────┘ └─────────────┘
```

### YARN Components

| Component | Role | Responsibility |
|-----------|------|-----------------|
| **ResourceManager** | Global | Resource allocation, scheduler |
| **ApplicationMaster** | Per-App | App lifecycle, negotiate resources |
| **NodeManager** | Per-Node | Container launch, monitor |
| **Container** | Task Unit | Isolated resource allocation |

