### 3. Parallelism Tuning

```java
public class ParallelismTuning {
    
    public static void tuneParallelism(Job job, Configuration conf, 
                                       long inputSize) {
        
        // Number of mappers = Number of input splits
        // Each split processed by one mapper
        long bytesPerMapper = 128 * 1024 * 1024; // 128 MB default
        int numMappers = (int) Math.ceil((double) inputSize / bytesPerMapper);
        
        // Number of reducers - usually 0.95 * cluster capacity
        int numReducers = conf.getInt("mapreduce.job.reduces", 1);
        
        // Ideal: 5-10 minutes per task
        // 30 second to 1 minute tasks too many
        // 5+ hour tasks too few
        
        // Configure
        job.setNumReduceTasks(Math.max(1, numReducers));
        
        // Slow start
        conf.setFloat("mapreduce.job.reduce.slowstart.completedmaps", 0.05f);
    }
}
```

