## 2. MapReduce Execution - Complete Concept

### **Theory: Job Execution Pipeline**

```
INPUT PHASE
├─ Read input file from HDFS
├─ Split into chunks based on InputFormat
└─ Create input split for each mapper

MAP PHASE (Parallel)
├─ Each mapper receives one split
├─ Process line-by-line (or custom record)
├─ Emit intermediate (key, value) pairs
└─ Spill to disk when buffer full

SHUFFLE & SORT PHASE (Automatic)
├─ Shuffle: Send all values for same key to one reducer
├─ Sort: Within reducer, sort by key
└─ Merge: Combine multiple mapper outputs

REDUCE PHASE (Parallel)
├─ Receive sorted groups of (key, values)
├─ Aggregate/process values for each key
├─ Emit final (key, value) pairs
└─ Write to HDFS

OUTPUT PHASE
└─ Store results in output directory
```

### **Memory Management During Execution**

```
MAPPER MEMORY ALLOCATION (e.g., 1024 MB)
├─ JVM Heap: 800 MB (from mapreduce.map.java.opts)
│   ├─ Code execution
│   ├─ User objects
│   └─ Collections (TreeMap for spill)
└─ System: 224 MB (overhead)

SORT BUFFER (spill-related)
├─ io.sort.mb: 100 MB (circular buffer)
├─ io.sort.spill.percent: 80% (spill at 80% full)
└─ io.sort.factor: 10 (merge 10 files at once)
```

### **Example: Word Count Flow**

```
Input File: "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog"

SPLIT PHASE:
Split 1: "The quick brown"
Split 2: "fox jumps over"
Split 3: "the lazy dog"

MAP PHASE:
Mapper 1:
  The → (The, 1)
  quick → (quick, 1)
  brown → (brown, 1)

Mapper 2:
  fox → (fox, 1)
  jumps → (jumps, 1)
  over → (over, 1)

Mapper 3:
  the → (the, 1)
  lazy → (lazy, 1)
  dog → (dog, 1)

SHUFFLE & SORT:
Group by key (case-insensitive):
brown: [1]
dog: [1]
fox: [1]
jumps: [1]
lazy: [1]
over: [1]
quick: [1]
the: [1, 1]
The: [1]

REDUCE PHASE:
brown: 1
dog: 1
fox: 1
jumps: 1
lazy: 1
over: 1
quick: 1
the: 2
The: 1
```

### **Keypoints to Remember**

✓ **Combiner = Local Reducer** - Runs on mapper, reduces data transfer
✓ **Shuffle is automatic** - No code needed, always happens
✓ **Sorted within partition** - All keys sorted within reducer input
✓ **Partitioner determines reducer** - Default uses hash(key) % numReducers
✓ **Spill = disk write** - When sort buffer gets full, spilled to disk

