## 7. Partitioner and Custom Partitioning - Complete Concept

### **Theory: Why Partitioners Matter**

```
DEFAULT PARTITIONER: hash(key) % numReducers
Result: Can cause 90% of data in one reducer (skew)

CUSTOM PARTITIONER: Domain-specific logic
Result: Balanced load across reducers
```

### **Example: Date-Based Partitioning**

```
SCENARIO: 1 year of sales data, 12 reducers (one per month)

DEFAULT HASH PARTITIONER:
Result: Jan=1%, Feb=15%, Mar=2%, ... (Unbalanced!)

CUSTOM RANGE PARTITIONER:
Extract month from date → Send to month reducer
Result: Perfect balance!

Implementation:
public class DatePartitioner extends Partitioner<Text, Text> {
    public int getPartition(Text key, Text value, int numPartitions) {
        String month = key.toString().substring(5, 7);
        int monthNum = Integer.parseInt(month) - 1;
        return monthNum % numPartitions;
    }
}
```

### **Keypoints to Remember**

✓ **Partitioner called per mapper output** - Performance matters
✓ **Return value < numPartitions** - Or IndexOutOfBounds
✓ **Return value >= 0** - Negative causes errors
✓ **Prevents reducer skew** - Ensures balanced load
✓ **All keys for partition → same reducer** - Ensures grouping

